  "definition": "Adrenaline is an active hormone made by the adrenal medulla that stimulates both major adrenergic signaling systems. It increases heart activity, narrows blood vessels throughout the body, relaxes the gastrointestinal tract, and widens the bronchi and cerebral blood vessels.",
